 "equipment_type": "High-pressure atomising humidifier (direct room)",
 "applies_to": "CAREL humiFog direct UA pumping stations with c.pHC controller, one or two humidification zones in the room.",
 "summary": "humiFog direct is CAREL's high-pressure water atomising humidifier for direct room humidification, with one or two zones. Its c.pHC controller has Modbus and BACnet built in: BACnet MS/TP on the RS485 BMS port or BACnet IP on the Ethernet port (BACnet is the Ethernet default). The object list holds alarm BVs, a unit status code, zone requests, production, water use, probe readings and per-zone set points.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names here are the manual's Variable column; the manual's Parameter column is used as the description.",
  "The manual prints three rows only as ranges: BV 24-31 (wireless probe 1-8 offline), BV 36-39 (unit 1-4 alarm) and AV 13-28 (wireless probe 1-8 humidity on odd instances 13-27, temperature on even instances 14-28). Each is listed here as one row at its first instance with the name as printed; the other instances exist but their names are not printed individually.",
  "Zone 2 objects only apply to two-zone cabinets; wireless probe objects only apply when CAREL wireless probes are installed.",
  "Units follow the unit's metric/imperial setting (%RH or °C/°F for probes, bar/psi, kg/h or lb/h). The manual prints % for the zone 2 humidity set points.",
  "Source: section 10.4 'List of BACnet parameters', page 32, Tab. 10.c (85 objects, printed as 61 rows because of the three ranges). The Italian edition is +0300073IT."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "humiFog direct - User manual",
  "doc_number": "+0300073EN rel. 1.4",
  "revision_date": "2022-03-29",
